{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbGn7398sgr8Ygzh3ccW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: APPROVE\n\nfmt, clippy `-D warnings` and `cargo test` all pass locally. Every acceptance criterion is covered by `tests/cli_info_e2e.rs`. The `models` criterion says \"thirteen\" but the ticket lists twelve; the PR says so, and the test asserts twelve.\n\nP3 src/doctor.rs:310 — `check_plugin_registration` option and the hardcoded all-true `plugin_registration` struct (lines 362-368, 405, 443) are dead shims \"kept so existing callers compile\". The #11 spec says the plugin-registration and legacy-name checks are gone. — Delete the field and the struct, and drop the `None` at `src/cli_info.rs:90`.\n\nP3 src/tool_schemas.rs:40 — The description still says \"resolved model family is 'claude'\", but `family` no longer exists. — Reword to \"backend\".\n\nP3 config/models.json:12-14 — The Claude cache-read prices look inconsistent: opus is 0.2 on a 4 input price, sonnet is 0.2 on 2, and fable is 0.25 on 10. I could not check them against list prices. — Check against Anthropic's list.\n\nP3 config/models.json:5-10 — The column alignment drifts across rows. — Reformat.\n\nP3 tests/cli_info_e2e.rs:50 — The test sets `CURSOR_DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`, but the spec renames it to `DELEGATE_HOST_PROFILE`. The rename ticket probably covers this. — Confirm that ticket picks it up.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5538,"cache_read_input_tokens":47463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5538},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1dbb4698-1c43-4b15-b933-765f45723b7a","uuid":"46227b39-84a5-4a13-a5b1-4c8f01387c6